00:55:05.530 --> 00:55:10.650
I'm so moved by that, but I also, I think I was 29 when we did the pilot.
我对此非常感动，但我也认为我们制作试播集时我才 29 岁。

00:55:10.650 --> 00:55:15.929
Maybe you were like 23 and I was 30 by the time we were actually doing it, or does that sound about right?
也许当我们真正开始做这件事的时候你才 23 岁，而我已经 30 岁了，或者这听起来对吗？

00:55:15.929 --> 00:55:21.969
But, you know, it's funny because I was like older than you, but this was also new for me.
但是，你知道，这很有趣，因为我比你年长，但这对我来说也是新的。

00:55:21.969 --> 00:56:03.336
I had never been on a big long-running TV show, I had done a bunch of pilots and so we were both in the trenches together and I think one of the ways I sometimes deal with my discomfort is I try to like be advicey and sage like and you know but you were I think we were figuring this thing out together and I have such a strong memory of seeing the first you've been the first time like walking down the hall when we were about to test together and I think that, you know, people have always remarked on our chemistry to the point where people insist that I was in love with you.
我从来没有参加过大型长期电视节目，我做过很多试播，所以我们都一起在战壕里，我想我有时处理我的不适的方式之一是我试着像智者一样提供建议，你知道，但你是我认为我们正在一起解决这个问题，我对第一次看到你有如此强烈的记忆，就像我们第一次一起走在大厅里，当我们准备一起测试时，我认为，你知道，人们总是评论我们的化学反应，以至于人们坚持认为我爱上了你。

00:56:03.336 --> 00:56:15.125
And I think you know that that was not true, but I did always feel like you and I had like, I don't know like we met on the first day of basic training or something.
我想你知道那不是真的，但我确实总觉得你和我有这样的感觉，我不知道我们是在基础训练的第一天见面的还是什么的。

00:56:15.125 --> 00:56:23.769
Like I felt like we were in the military together and we went through like this life changer together, like side by side.
我感觉就像我们一起在军队里一样，我们一起经历了人生的改变，就像肩并肩一样。

00:56:23.769 --> 00:56:27.650
And I, you know, sometimes people would ask about chemistry, did you ever discuss chemistry?
我，你知道，有时人们会问化学，你讨论过化学吗？

00:56:27.650 --> 00:56:29.250
And I'd be like, God, no.
我会说，上帝，不。

00:56:29.250 --> 00:56:32.369
Like I don't, that would be the worst thing you could ever do.
就像我不一样，那将是你能做的最糟糕的事情。

00:56:32.369 --> 00:56:42.409
Like I just had a sense that scenes with you and I were gonna be really honest and they were gonna be really thoughtful and we were gonna listen really well together.
就像我有一种感觉，与你和我一起的场景会非常诚实，他们会非常体贴，我们会一起很好地倾听。

00:56:42.409 --> 00:56:46.610
And I also thought, you know, Jordana made this point about your character, especially in the first season.
我还想，你知道，乔丹娜对你的角色提出了这一点，尤其是在第一季。

00:56:46.610 --> 00:56:58.502
There's a psychological term called tantalizing object, which is like the thing that like you really want, but it's just out of reach, and you can't quite have it, and we all have that romantically.
心理学上有一个术语叫“诱人的对象”，就像你真正想要的东西，但它只是遥不可及，你无法完全拥有它，而我们都浪漫地拥有它。

00:56:58.502 --> 00:57:06.250
And I think one thing that I think is fascinating is you met Taryn right before we started this thing, and you're still with him.
我认为一件令人着迷的事情是你在我们开始这件事之前遇到了塔伦，而且你仍然和他在一起。

00:57:06.250 --> 00:57:20.230
So you yourself were not, we didn't have these attachment theory terms when we were doing the show, but like Craig and I have talked that Ted has an anxious attachment wound, And Robin has an avoidant attachment wound.
所以你自己不是，我们在做节目时没有这些依恋理论术语，但就像克雷格和我所说的那样，泰德有焦虑型依恋伤口，罗宾有回避型依恋伤口。

00:57:20.230 --> 00:57:29.829
But in real life, actually, we were reversed because you were in this really serious long-term relationship that you're still in.
但在现实生活中，实际上，我们被逆转了，因为你仍然处于这种非常认真的长期关系中。

00:57:29.829 --> 00:57:37.070
And I was actually, as you remember from many of our off-stage talks, really confused about relationships, like how I couldn't stay in them.
事实上，正如你从我们的许多台下谈话中所记得的那样，我对人际关系感到非常困惑，就像我如何无法留在其中一样。

00:57:37.070 --> 00:57:42.349
I didn't know how long if I wanted to be in them, if I wanted to ever get married, I've worked through all that.
我不知道我是否想加入他们多久，如果我想结婚，我已经经历了这一切。

00:57:42.349 --> 00:57:54.269
But I find it fascinating that we were both navigating like love and romance at that time in our lives, but from totally different perspectives than our characters.
但我觉得很有趣的是，我们在生活中的那个时候都像爱情和浪漫一样航行，但角度与我们的角色完全不同。

00:57:54.269 --> 00:58:09.349
But I don't know, there was just something about, when people ask like if we're friends, like with the cast, I say sure, but it's actually family is a better analogy because you don't get to choose your family.
但我不知道，当人们问我们是不是朋友，就像演员一样，我说当然，但实际上家庭是一个更好的类比，因为你无法选择你的家庭。

00:58:09.349 --> 00:58:10.869
You're just thrown together.
你们只是被扔在一起。

00:58:10.869 --> 00:58:14.150
and you have to kind of make this ecosystem work.
你必须让这个生态系统发挥作用。

00:58:14.150 --> 00:58:22.309
And, you know, there were, set was different when you and I had a one-on-one scene than it was five of us at the bar.
而且，你知道，当你和我进行一对一的场景时，场景与我们五个人在酒吧时的场景有所不同。

00:58:22.309 --> 00:58:32.750
Or you and Neil together, or me and Jason and Ali, like there were so many different configurations that changed the energy of what the day was gonna be like.
或者你和尼尔在一起，或者我和杰森和阿里在一起，就像有很多不同的配置改变了这一天的能量。

00:58:32.750 --> 00:58:43.579
But I do, you know, in some ways like if it's the Wizard of Oz, like you were the Scarecrow for me, like you were like the first person I met on the journey.
但我确实，你知道，在某些方面，就像是绿野仙踪，就像你是我的稻草人，就像你是我在旅途中遇到的第一个人。

00:58:43.579 --> 00:58:45.340
And I just like, I love you very much.
我只是喜欢，我非常爱你。

00:58:45.340 --> 00:58:47.960
And I just, I just want to say that.
我只是，我只想这么说。

00:58:47.960 --> 00:58:49.320
Say it, buddy.
说吧，伙计。

00:58:49.320 --> 00:58:50.239
Oh, are you guys?
哦，你们是吗？

00:58:50.239 --> 00:58:51.079
I love you both.
我爱你们俩。

00:58:52.380 --> 00:58:53.480
It's, what a gift.
这真是一份礼物。

00:58:53.480 --> 00:58:55.880
How lucky were, how lucky were slash are we?
我们有多幸运，斜线有多幸运？

00:58:55.880 --> 00:58:56.719
I mean, just.
我的意思是，只是。

00:58:56.719 --> 00:58:57.534
Oh, lucky.
哦，幸运的是。

00:58:57.534 --> 00:58:58.920
We were so lucky.
我们太幸运了。

00:58:58.920 --> 00:59:03.679
Like it's so, it's such a, it was such an amazing time.
就这样，这真是一段美妙的时光。

00:59:04.639 --> 00:59:06.280
And just, I miss it.
只是，我很想念它。

00:59:06.280 --> 00:59:11.739
Like I don't like, I don't really miss people go like, What do you miss most of the show and of like the people?
就像我不喜欢，我并不真正想念人们一样，你最想念节目和喜欢的人的什么？

00:59:11.739 --> 00:59:13.739
Like being able to just go in.
就像可以直接进去一样。

00:59:13.739 --> 00:59:20.019
And I think you've touched upon this in your podcast already, which is like life happened.
我认为您已经在播客中谈到了这一点，这就像生活发生过一样。

00:59:20.019 --> 00:59:25.019
Like people got married, people met their partners, people divorced their partners.
就像人们结婚一样，人们遇到他们的伴侣，人们与他们的伴侣离婚。

00:59:25.019 --> 00:59:26.900
We have people pass away, you know?
我们有人去世了，你知道吗？

00:59:26.900 --> 00:59:27.739
It was like.
就像。

00:59:27.739 --> 00:59:28.579
Yeah.
是的。

00:59:28.579 --> 00:59:29.820
And we all went through some shit.
我们都经历过一些糟糕的事情。

00:59:29.820 --> 00:59:31.820
We all went through some journeys and some shit.
我们都经历过一些旅程，也经历过一些狗屎。

00:59:31.820 --> 00:59:32.659
Yeah.
是的。

00:59:32.659 --> 00:59:33.659
We really did.
我们真的做到了。

00:59:33.659 --> 00:59:37.260
And so it's, it's, that made it in there too.
所以它也在那里。

00:59:37.260 --> 00:59:39.539
It's just, it was like a lifetime.
只是，就这样过了一辈子。

00:59:39.539 --> 00:59:42.880
And when I even say like, we, and people ask like, how many seasons did you do?
当我这样说时，我们和人们会问，你拍了几季？

00:59:42.880 --> 00:59:44.840
I was like, we did nine seasons.
我当时想，我们拍了九季。

00:59:44.840 --> 00:59:46.500
We did nine years.
我们做了九年。

00:59:46.500 --> 00:59:49.380
Like, call it a decade of our life, call it a decade.
就像，称之为我们生命的十年，称之为十年。

00:59:49.380 --> 00:59:50.219
And we were all living life.
我们都过着生活。

00:59:50.219 --> 00:59:57.199
The other thing though, I think someone to think about is like, everyone sees 22 to 24 minutes of that week that we spent together.
不过，我认为需要考虑的另一件事是，每个人都会看到我们一起度过的那一周的 22 到 24 分钟。

00:59:57.199 --> 00:59:58.780
But how many hours were we together?
但我们在一起有多少小时？

00:59:58.780 --> 01:00:02.219
Like, most of our life was happening not on screen.
就像，我们生活的大部分时间都不是在屏幕上发生的。

01:00:02.219 --> 01:00:04.539
Like, even on set life.
就像，即使是在片场生活。

01:00:04.539 --> 01:00:07.579
And people think like, oh, no, it's the five of you.
人们会想，哦，不，是你们五个人。

01:00:07.579 --> 01:00:11.340
And we try to remind people on the podcast, no, it was 75 of us.
我们试图在播客上提醒人们，不，我们有 75 个人。

01:00:11.340 --> 01:00:13.739
There were so many people around.
周围有很多人。

01:00:13.739 --> 01:00:18.219
And so many people you get really close to.
还有很多你非常亲近的人。

01:00:18.219 --> 01:00:23.460
Jen, Turkey didn't even do my makeup, but we're still in touch.
Jen，土耳其甚至没有给我化妆，但我们仍然保持联系。

01:00:23.460 --> 01:00:27.340
I just adore her and I gave a toast at her wedding.
我很喜欢她，我在她的婚礼上祝酒。

01:00:27.340 --> 01:00:42.789
You really get woven into people's lives in a way that is not, the public's never gonna get how intimate and how sweet a well-functioning set can be.
你真的以一种不是的方式融入了人们的生活，公众永远不会意识到一个运作良好的场景可以有多么亲密和甜蜜。

01:00:42.989 --> 01:00:46.789
But they do, I think they don't know it, but they feel it in the show.
但他们确实如此，我想他们自己不知道，但他们在节目中感受到了。

01:00:46.789 --> 01:00:47.789
Because it shows up on screen.
因为它显示在屏幕上。

01:00:47.789 --> 01:00:49.170
That made it into this show.
这使它进入了这个节目。

01:00:49.170 --> 01:00:54.469
I don't know that it makes, it's not like that on every creative endeavor, but this one, it just filtered in.
我不知道它是否会产生这样的效果，并不是每一项创造性的努力都是如此，但是这一次，它只是渗透进来了。

01:00:54.469 --> 01:01:00.949
I just had this sense memory of this feeling of walking down to set, as I'm looking at the two of you loving you and missing you, but guys both.
当我看着你们两个爱着你们、想念你们的时候，我对这种走下片场的感觉有一种感觉记忆，但你们俩都是。

01:01:00.949 --> 01:01:11.710
and like, just this feeling of missing working with you, I mean, walking down the set, knowing I was gonna get to shoot, let's say that scene in the slutty pumpkin, the two of you up on the roof.
就像，就是怀念和你一起工作的感觉，我的意思是，走下片场，知道我要开始拍摄，比方说，放荡的南瓜中的场景，你们两个在屋顶上。

01:01:11.710 --> 01:01:21.269
Or that scene at the end of episode two of the Purple Giraffe where Robin sort of is saying, essentially, Kobe, what we started this podcast with, which is, can I be part of your group?
或者《紫色长颈鹿》第二集结尾处的场景，罗宾基本上是在说，科比，我们开始这个播客的目的是，我可以成为你们团队的一员吗？

01:01:21.269 --> 01:01:26.670
She's saying, I know I'm not saying I'm gonna date you, but it's too bad because I don't have friends here.
她说，我知道我不是说要和你约会，但这太糟糕了，因为我在这里没有朋友。

01:01:26.670 --> 01:01:32.360
And there's this wonderful moment where Ted says, come down with us at the bar tonight, you know?
在这个美妙的时刻，特德说，今晚和我们一起去酒吧吧，你知道吗？

01:01:32.360 --> 01:01:37.159
It was like, he said, maybe in a couple months, we'll talk and she's like, and Robin's heartbroken for second, she knows it's not gonna happen.
他说，就像，也许几个月后，我们会谈谈，她就像，罗宾心碎了，她知道这不会发生。

01:01:37.159 --> 01:01:39.559
Then he says, or tonight, come down, Drake, with us tonight.
然后他说，或者今晚，德雷克，今晚和我们一起下来。

01:01:39.559 --> 01:01:44.440
It's this lovely moment where she's invited into the group and it felt like you being invited into the show.
在这个可爱的时刻，她被邀请加入这个团体，感觉就像你被邀请参加演出一样。

01:01:44.440 --> 01:01:49.639
And just like, knowing I got to go shoot scenes with the two of you, I mean, what a gift is a writer.
就像，知道我必须和你们两个一起去拍摄场景，我的意思是，作家是多么有天赋啊。

01:01:49.639 --> 01:01:51.760
I know Carter very much felt the same way.
我知道卡特也有同样的感觉。

01:01:51.760 --> 01:01:55.719
It's just like, I get to go shoot a scene with these two today on that roof.
就像，我今天要去那个屋顶上拍摄这两个人的场景。

01:01:55.719 --> 01:01:57.920
It's going to be fucking great.
这将会非常棒。

01:01:57.920 --> 01:02:01.159
And it's just what is the best writing gets?
这就是最好的写作吗？

01:02:01.159 --> 01:02:03.079
It's the best making something gets is that feeling.
做某事最好的就是那种感觉。

01:02:03.079 --> 01:02:04.039
So thank you guys.
所以谢谢你们。

01:02:04.039 --> 01:02:04.880
What a gift.
多么好的礼物啊。

01:02:04.880 --> 01:02:05.719
Thank you.
谢谢。

01:02:05.719 --> 01:02:06.559
Thank you, Mark.
谢谢你，马克。

01:02:06.559 --> 01:02:07.400
Yeah, we love you.
是的，我们爱你。

01:02:07.400 --> 01:02:11.199
We all, Carter and I, we're just the luckiest writers and all of the writers and the world to bring to you guys.
我们所有人，卡特和我，都是最幸运的作家，也是所有作家和全世界带给你们的幸运。

01:02:11.199 --> 01:02:12.039
Doings, mutual.
所做的事，相互的。

01:02:12.039 --> 01:02:13.239
Kobe, we adore you.
科比，我们崇拜你。

01:02:13.239 --> 01:02:15.119
We talk about you every week.
我们每周都会谈论你。

01:02:15.119 --> 01:02:16.159
Will you come back soon?
你会很快回来吗？

01:02:16.159 --> 01:02:18.960
We'll get an episode, a juicy Robin episode.
我们会得到一集，精彩的罗宾集。

01:02:18.960 --> 01:02:21.519
I know I get to come back for the Robin Sparkles one.
我知道我会回来找罗宾·斯帕克斯的。

01:02:21.519 --> 01:02:23.199
I mean, we're going to have a lot.
我的意思是，我们将会有很多。

01:02:23.199 --> 01:02:24.880
We didn't even really touch upon that.
我们甚至没有真正触及这一点。

01:02:24.880 --> 01:02:27.400
And I'm going to- Who wants you back for that one?
我要——谁想要你回来参加那个？

01:02:27.400 --> 01:02:28.870
We got to be reunited.
我们必须重聚。

01:02:28.870 --> 01:02:32.681
Yeah, I mean, and he's going to talk some shit about you.
是的，我是说，他会说一些关于你的坏话。

01:02:32.681 --> 01:02:35.824
He's got some, he says, you're on social media.
他说，他有一些，你在社交媒体上。

01:02:35.824 --> 01:02:41.240
And I'd be honest, you know, right there, but he's really difficult to work with.
老实说，你知道，就在那里，但他真的很难共事。

01:02:41.240 --> 01:02:50.400
He was telling us what you were whispering in his ear right before he'd seen the worst guest or I think we had on the show, to be honest.
老实说，在他看到最糟糕的客人之前，或者我认为我们在节目中遇到过的最糟糕的客人之前，他正在告诉我们你在他耳边低声说的话。

01:02:50.400 --> 01:02:56.719
No, that was, no, no, no, no, honestly, thank you guys.
不，那是，不，不，不，不，老实说，谢谢你们。

01:02:56.719 --> 01:03:12.119
Thank you guys for starting this podcast because it's so nice to jump into a time in my life where it was just, it was so fun and worked with such amazing people and just revisiting all these memories, you know, of, of times gone by.
谢谢你们开始这个播客，因为很高兴能进入我生命中的一段时光，那段时光非常有趣，与如此出色的人一起工作，并重温所有这些记忆，你知道，过去的时光。

01:03:12.119 --> 01:03:14.679
It's, it's, it's a wonderful, it's a wonderful journey.
这是，这是，这是一次美妙的旅程，这是一次美妙的旅程。

01:03:14.679 --> 01:03:15.679
So thank you.
所以谢谢你。

01:03:15.679 --> 01:03:16.519
Yeah.
是的。

01:03:16.519 --> 01:03:23.440
I actually texted Alec and Craig because I had this revelation that like, we're kind of doing an oral history of how I met your mother.
事实上，我给亚历克和克雷格发了短信，因为我得到了这样的启示，我们正在口述我是如何认识你母亲的。

01:03:23.440 --> 01:03:30.000
Like we're going back and we're unearthing these memories and these revelations that we've had.
就像我们要回去，我们正在挖掘我们所拥有的这些记忆和这些启示。

01:03:30.000 --> 01:03:35.039
I mean, one of the things is like, the show is a lot about time and change.
我的意思是，其中一件事是，这部剧很大程度上是关于时间和变化的。

01:03:35.039 --> 01:03:38.760
And when we made the show, we were one way.
当我们制作这部剧时，我们是一种方式。

01:03:38.760 --> 01:03:44.079
First season, when we ended the show, we were different, our lives looked different, our everything looked different.
第一季，当我们结束演出时，我们不同了，我们的生活看起来不同了，我们的一切看起来都不同了。

01:03:44.079 --> 01:03:50.960
And now, 11 years on from the ending of the show, 20 years on from when we started, things also look a lot different.
现在，距离这部剧结束已经过去了 11 年，距离我们开始播出也已经过去了 20 年，事情看起来也有了很大的不同。

01:03:50.960 --> 01:03:57.360
I mean, it's an astonishing thing to grow with a piece of art and have it change as we change.
我的意思是，与一件艺术品一起成长并随着我们的改变而改变，这是一件令人惊讶的事情。

01:03:57.360 --> 01:03:58.599
And that's what we're doing here.
这就是我们在这里所做的。

01:03:58.599 --> 01:04:05.800
And you, this show is not anything, I mean, it's unimaginable without you.
而你，这个节目什么都不是，我的意思是，没有你，这是难以想象的。

01:04:05.800 --> 01:04:10.159
So we want to have you back, we want to keep talking about it, and we both love you.
所以我们想让你回来，我们想继续谈论它，我们都爱你。

01:04:10.159 --> 01:04:11.159
